        "faq-title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
        "faq-subtitle": "Answers to the most common inquiries about investments and wealth management in Panama",
        "faq-q1": "How can a foreigner invest in Panama?",
        "faq-a1": "Panama offers multiple avenues for foreign investors, from the stock market and real estate to residency-by-investment programs. The process begins with opening an investment or bank account, for which Wealth Trust Partners acts as your strategic bridge to regulated institutions.",
        "faq-q2": "What are the benefits of investing in Panama?",
        "faq-a2": "Key benefits include a dollarized economy, political stability, a territorial tax system (no taxes on income earned outside Panama), and a strategic geographical location connecting global markets.",
        "faq-q3": "What types of investments are most profitable in Panama?",
        "faq-a3": "Historically, commercial real estate, local investment funds, and fixed-income instruments have shown solid returns. Panama is also a growing hub for technology and digital asset investments.",
        "faq-q4": "Is it safe to invest in Panama as a foreigner?",
        "faq-a4": "Yes, Panama has a robust legal framework that protects private property and foreign investment. The International Banking Center is highly regulated, providing a secure and transparent environment for global capital.",
        "faq-q5": "How to open a bank account in Panama as a foreigner?",
        "faq-a5": "Opening an account requires documentation proving the source of funds, bank and personal references, and a valid passport. At WTP, we assist in the collection and pre-approval of documents to facilitate the process with custodian banks.",
        "faq-q6": "What documents do I need to open an investment account in Panama?",
        "faq-a6": "Generally required: passport copy, a second ID, proof of address, tax returns or financial statements validating the source of wealth, and bank references.",
        "faq-q7": "Can I open an account in Panama without traveling?",
        "faq-a7": "Depending on the institution and the client's profile, some processes can be started remotely through video interviews and sending apostilled documents. However, for certain final products, physical presence or formal legal representation is recommended.",
        "faq-q8": "What is a Panamanian trust and how does it protect my assets?",
        "faq-a8": "A trust is a legal contract where assets are transferred to a trustee to be managed for the benefit of beneficiaries. It offers protection against seizures and litigation, ensuring the wealth is maintained for the purposes established by the settlor.",
        "faq-q9": "What is the difference between a trust and a private interest foundation?",
        "faq-a9": "A foundation is its own legal entity (similar to a living trust), while a trust is a contract. Both serve protection and succession purposes, but the choice depends on the complexity of assets and privacy goals.",
        "faq-q10": "How to incorporate a corporation in Panama?",
        "faq-a10": "A resident agent (Panamanian lawyer) and a minimum of three directors are required. The process is agile and allows for foreign shareholders, maintaining a high level of operational flexibility.",
        "faq-q11": "What is Panama's territorial tax system and how does it benefit me?",
        "faq-a11": "It means Panama only taxes income produced within the country. If you have a Panamanian corporation generating income from business outside the territory, that income is exempt from local taxes.",
        "faq-q12": "Does Panama charge taxes on foreign income?",
        "faq-a12": "No. Income derived from commercial operations, investments, or dividends obtained outside Panama is not subject to income tax in Panama.",
        "faq-q13": "What investor visas does Panama offer?",
        "faq-a13": "Primary options include the Qualified Investor Visa (fast permanent residency), the Friendly Nations Visa, and the Self-Economic Solvency Visa.",
        "faq-q14": "What is the Friendly Nations Visa?",
        "faq-a14": "It is a special immigration regime for citizens of countries with close ties to Panama, allowing for permanent residency through a real estate investment or a fixed-term deposit.",
        "faq-q15": "How can foreign companies benefit from Panama?",
        "faq-a15": "They can establish regional headquarters (SEM), use free zones with special tax incentives, or simply operate from Panama to optimize their logistics and global treasury in dollars.",
        "faq-q16": "Are Panamanian trusts unseizable?",
        "faq-a16": "Under Law 1 of 1984, trust assets constitute a separate patrimony from the trustee and the settlor, and cannot be seized for the latter's obligations, except in cases of proven fraud.",
